  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2f4848e7e46289243b311920bdbdddf0, type: 3}
  m_Name: Abacus
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  playerLines:
  - An abacus huh...
  - What's that?
  - That sounds quite useful
  - Though we have calculators now instead
  - <i>hmm...</i>
  - <i>So using operations apply those operations on a number</i>
  - <i>If this number is large enough, it can overwhelm an opponent</i>
  NPCLines:
  - It's a tool that was used millenia ago by ancient people
  - They were used to assist in counting and simple calculations
  - The first abacus appeared in ancient Mesopotamia but looked very different to
    the abacus we're used to now
  - The first abacus was in base 60 and allowed the calculation of very large numbers
  - These large numbers could get very overwhelming very quickly depending on the
    operations performed
  - Remember, if you're ever in a tight spot, try applying whatever powerful operations
    you can to overwhelm your opponent
  - Operations can come in several types and have a variety of effects on whatever
    number you want
  speakTurnPlayer: 0101000000010100000000010101
